    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d442">

                <pb facs="0382" n="370" sameAs="frus:frus1942v04/pg370"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">882.20/561</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Harry A. McBride, Special Representative of
                        President Roosevelt in Liberia, to the President of Liberia</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Barclay</hi>)<anchor n="17" xml:id="d442-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Monrovia</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-03-20">March 20, 1942</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. President</hi>: With reference to the
                    credit in the amount of $1,000,000, which is to be established for Liberia by
                    the United States Government it is my understanding that the Liberian Government
                    will make use of the credit for defense purposes in the following manner: <list>
                        <label>1.</label>
                        <item>Approximately $150,000 for the payment locally of an increased
                            Frontier Force;</item>
                        <label>2.</label>
                        <item>Approximately $200,000 to be expended by the United States War
                            Department in the construction of an access road between the Roberts
                            Field Airport and Fisherman Lake;</item>
                        <label>3.</label>
                        <item>Approximately $600,000 for the construction of permanent roads, such
                            construction to be performed under a contract which would be granted to
                            an American firm considered competent for the purpose by the United
                            States War Department, employing the machinery which has been used in
                            the construction of Roberts Field Airport and which will be turned over
                            for the construction of Liberian roads;</item>
                        <label>4.</label>
                        <item>The remainder to be used for further equipment of the Frontier Force
                            for such items as, uniforms, housing, sustenance et cetera, and for
                            improving Liberian radio communications.</item>
                    </list>
                </p>
                <p>It will be gratefully appreciated if you will be good enough to confirm this
                    understanding if it is in accord with your wishes.<anchor n="18"
                        xml:id="d442-f2"/>
                </p>
                <p>Sincerely,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>H. A. <hi rendition="#small-caps">McBride</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d442-f1" n="17" type="source" xml:id="d442-f1-content">
                <p>Copies of this letter and the two letters <hi rendition="#italic">infra</hi> were
                    handed to the Assistant Chief of the Division of Near Eastern Affairs (Villard)
                    by Mr. McBride upon his return from Liberia.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d442-f2" n="18" xml:id="d442-f2-content">
                <p>Mr. McBride subsequently indicated that there was no reply from President
                    Barclay.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
